<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal non-EU trade deficit rises in March.</title>
<headline>Portugal non-EU trade deficit rises in March.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's trade deficit with countries outside the European Union (EU) rose 11.9 percent to 55.6 billion escudos in March, compared with February, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the latest figures:</p>
<p>				MAR 97  FEB 97  MAR 96</p>
<p>IMPORTS		     116.3   105.7   114.3</p>
<p>EXPORTS			60.7    56.0    66.6</p>
<p>DEFICIT			55.6    49.7    47.7</p>
<p>COVERAGE RATE	    52.2 pct 53.0 pct 58.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 figures definitive; 1997 figures preliminary</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
